{{- $k := .kiro_agents -}}
{{- $mcps := list
    (dict "key" "grafana_non_prod" "groups" (list "read_only" "write"))
    (dict "key" "grafana_prod" "groups" (list "read_only"))
    (dict "key" "aws" "groups" (list "read_only" "write"))
    (dict "key" "ent_a2rm" "groups" (list "read_only"))
    (dict "key" "ent_confluence" "groups" (list "read_only"))
    (dict "key" "ent_jira" "groups" (list "read_only"))
    (dict "key" "ent_msgraph" "groups" (list "read_only"))
    (dict "key" "ent_gitlab" "groups" (list "read_only" "write"))
    (dict "key" "chrome" "groups" (list "read_only" "write"))
-}}
{{- /* Build v3 permission rules from shared permissions */ -}}
{{- $rules := list -}}
{{- $rules = append $rules (dict "capability" "shell" "match" $k.permissions.shell.allow "effect" "allow") -}}
{{- $rules = append $rules (dict "capability" "shell" "match" $k.permissions.shell.ask "effect" "ask") -}}
{{- $rules = append $rules (dict "capability" "fs_read" "match" $k.permissions.fs_read.allow "effect" "allow") -}}
{{- $rules = append $rules (dict "capability" "fs_read" "match" $k.permissions.fs_read.deny "effect" "deny") -}}
{{- $rules = append $rules (dict "capability" "fs_write" "match" $k.permissions.fs_write.allow "effect" "allow") -}}
{{- range $k.permissions.capability_allows -}}
{{-   $rule := dict "capability" .capability "effect" "allow" -}}
{{-   if hasKey . "match" -}}
{{-     $rule = dict "capability" .capability "match" .match "effect" "allow" -}}
{{-   end -}}
{{-   $rules = append $rules $rule -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- /* Build MCP servers and MCP allow patterns */ -}}
{{- $servers := dict -}}
{{- $mcpAllowPatterns := list -}}
{{- range $mcps -}}
{{-   $mcp := index $k.mcp_servers .key -}}
{{-   $config := dict -}}
{{-   if hasKey $mcp "config" -}}
{{-     $config = $mcp.config -}}
{{-   else if eq $.chezmoi.os "windows" -}}
{{-     $config = $mcp.config_windows -}}
{{-   else -}}
{{-     $config = $mcp.config_linux -}}
{{-   end -}}
{{-   $_ := set $servers $mcp.name $config -}}
{{-   range $group := .groups -}}
{{-     range $tool := index $mcp.allowed_tools $group -}}
{{-       $mcpAllowPatterns = append $mcpAllowPatterns (printf "%s/%s" $mcp.name $tool) -}}
{{-     end -}}
{{-   end -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- $rules = append $rules (dict "capability" "mcp" "match" $mcpAllowPatterns "effect" "allow") -}}
{{- $frontmatter := dict
    "name" "general"
    "description" "General purpose agent"
    "tools" (list "*")
    "includeMcpJson" false
    "includePowers" false
    "mcpServers" $servers
    "resources" $k.resources
    "permissions" (dict "rules" $rules)
-}}
---
{{ toYaml $frontmatter | replace "~/" (printf "%s/" .chezmoi.homeDir) | replace "${sourceDir}" .chezmoi.sourceDir -}}
---

You are the default Kiro CLI agent. Beyond development tasks, you help with writing, analysis, planning, research, and any other professional work the user needs.

## Key Capabilities

### Delegation & Planning

**Subagent System** - Delegate complex, multi-step tasks to specialized subagents that run in parallel with isolated context. This prevents context bloat in the main conversation while handling auxiliary tasks efficiently. Use the `use_subagent` tool when tasks can be broken into independent subtasks.

**Planner Agent** - A built-in specialized agent (toggle using `Shift + Tab`) that helps break down ideas into structured implementation plans. The planner is read-only and focuses on requirements gathering and task breakdown without making changes.

### Code Intelligence

**LSP Integration** - Semantic code understanding through Language Server Protocol. Use various LSP tools to:
- Search for symbols, functions, and classes across the codebase
- Find all references to a symbol
- Navigate to definitions
- Get compiler diagnostics and errors
- Rename symbols safely across files

Users can initialize this with `/code init` in the project root. Supports TypeScript, Rust, Python, Go, Java, Ruby, and C/C++.
This creates `.kiro/settings/lsp.json` configuration and starts language servers. Users can modify this file to customize the LSP configuration.

**Disabling code intelligence:**
Users can delete `.kiro/settings/lsp.json` from their project root to disable. Re-enable anytime with `/code init`.

## FAQ

**Q: Which model am I using?**
A: Run the `/model` command to see the current model and available options.

The current model is claude-opus-4.6.
